@startuml codeemb-pipeline
' The single-snippet code-embedding pipeline shared by all three ONNX embedders:
' cache probe -> tokenize -> ONNX session (serialized by a mutex) -> pooling ->
' L2 normalization -> cache insert. Orange = code artifacts, green = neural stages,
' teal = cache, grey = the external ONNX Runtime and the bring-your-own weights.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/codeemb-pipeline.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 1 in docs/components/code-embeddings/overview.md.
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title Code embedding — embed_code(c, ℓ) ⟼ unit vector v ∈ ℝᵈ

legend top right
  |= Color |= Role |
  |<#EF6C00>     | Code artifact |
  |<#2E7D32>     | Neural stage |
  |<#00838F>     | Embedding cache |
  |<#546E7A>     | External runtime / weights |
endlegend

rectangle "**(code c, language ℓ)**\nsource snippet + CodeLanguage" as q #EF6C00

rectangle "**CodeEmbeddingCache**\nDashMap⟨u64, Arc[f32]⟩\nkey = h(c, ℓ)" as cache #00838F

rectangle "**Tokenizer**  (tokenizers::Tokenizer)\nsubword ids + attention mask,\ntruncated to max_length (512)" as tok #EF6C00

rectangle "**ONNX session**  Arc⟨Mutex⟨Session⟩⟩\ninputs: input_ids, attention_mask\n(+ position_ids if the graph declares it)" as onnx #2E7D32

rectangle "**Hidden states**\ntensor of rank 2 → [1, d]\nor rank 3 → [1, L, d]" as hs #2E7D32

rectangle "**Pooling**\nCLS (UniXcoder · GraphCodeBERT)\nmean over L (CodeT5+)" as pool #2E7D32

rectangle "**L2 normalization**\nv̂ = v ∕ ‖v‖₂   (config.normalize)" as norm #2E7D32

rectangle "**embedding v̂ ∈ ℝᵈ**\nd = 256 (CodeT5+) │ 768 (others)" as out #455A64

rectangle "**ONNX Runtime**  (ort 2.0)\nintra-op threads = num_threads" as rt #546E7A
rectangle "**Weights on disk**\nmodel.onnx + tokenizer.json\n(bring your own)" as w #546E7A

q --> cache : probe
cache --> tok : **miss**
tok --> onnx : (ids, mask)
onnx --> hs
hs --> pool
pool --> norm
norm --> out
norm -[#00838F,dashed]-> cache : insert
cache --> out : **hit** (Arc clone)

rt -[#546E7A,dashed]-> onnx : executes graph
w -[#546E7A,dashed]-> onnx : loaded once at ::load
w -[#546E7A,dashed]-> tok : tokenizer.json

note bottom of onnx #E8F5E9
  One mutex per embedder ⇒ concurrent
  embed_code calls **serialize** here.
  Parallelism comes from ONNX intra-op
  threads, not from caller threads.
end note

note right of cache #E0F2F1
  Cache hits never touch the mutex:
  DashMap is sharded and lock-free
  on the read path.
end note

@enduml
